WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:05.756
In this video, you will see how you choose a contest pass, before your contest goes live.

00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:06.764
We start on the map.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.394
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:12.255 --> 00:00:14.805
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:17.461
Then tap Allow.

00:00:19.035 --> 00:00:21.128
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:21.128 --> 00:00:25.054
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:26.607 --> 00:00:31.399
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:35.490
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.273
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:38.273 --> 00:00:42.836
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:43.537
Tap it.

00:00:46.066 --> 00:00:49.066
In the menu, tap Add an event, home or contest.

00:00:51.678 --> 00:00:56.430
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own home.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.072
This is the Add page.

00:00:58.072 --> 00:00:59.680
It has three choices.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.275
An event, like a tree lighting or a holiday parade.

00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:08.171
A contest, where neighbors enter their homes, and the community votes for a favorite.

00:01:08.171 --> 00:01:10.858
Or a lighting display, to show off your own home.

00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:14.310
We are creating a contest, so tap A contest.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.358
First, the name.

00:01:17.358 --> 00:01:23.575
This is the title everyone sees, on the contest page, on the map, and in the emails your neighbors get.

00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:29.074
Something simple and local works best, like your street or neighborhood, and the year.

00:01:29.074 --> 00:01:32.492
I will type Oak Hill Holiday Lights 2027.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.653
Then tap Next.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.800
Next, who is running it, and where.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.454
Type the name of your group.

00:01:39.454 --> 00:01:45.769
It can be a city, a school, an H O A, a club, a business, or just your neighbors on one street.

00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:47.802
Then pick the city the homes are in.

00:01:47.802 --> 00:01:50.815
That is how your contest shows up for the right neighbors.

00:01:50.815 --> 00:01:51.652
Tap Next.

00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:55.474
This is the welcome message.

00:01:55.474 --> 00:02:01.507
Neighbors read it before they decide to enter, so it is your chance to say what the contest is about.

00:02:01.507 --> 00:02:03.589
We already wrote a friendly one for you.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:07.469
You can keep it as it is, or change a few words so it sounds like you.

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:08.320
Tap Next.

00:02:09.987 --> 00:02:11.831
A website is optional.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:17.035
If your group has one, add it here, and people can see who is behind the contest.

00:02:17.035 --> 00:02:21.140
Your contest goes live right away either way, so it is fine to skip this.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:21.979
Tap Next.

00:02:23.688 --> 00:02:24.470
Now the dates.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:25.489
There are three.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:27.884
The last day neighbors can enter.

00:02:27.884 --> 00:02:29.302
The day voting starts.

00:02:29.302 --> 00:02:30.641
And the day voting ends.

00:02:32.594 --> 00:02:36.641
Entries and voting open and close on these dates by themselves.

00:02:36.641 --> 00:02:39.749
We filled in typical dates, so you can just tap Next.

00:02:41.303 --> 00:02:43.929
You can change any of them later, from your dashboard.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.778
Choose Quick start, then tap Next.

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:50.550
This is the review.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:56.454
Your organization has no pass yet, so the passes appear right here, before the contest goes live.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.608
The page says where your organization stands in its 12-month window.

00:03:01.608 --> 00:03:06.144
You have no pass running yet, so choose one to start your contest.

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:12.079
There are three passes: a single contest, up to 5 contests, and up to 20 contests.

00:03:12.079 --> 00:03:14.962
The number counts every contest in your window.

00:03:14.962 --> 00:03:18.815
Each card lists everything it gives you, and the price is on the card.

00:03:21.238 --> 00:03:23.511
Running more than twenty contests?

00:03:23.511 --> 00:03:25.865
The Up to 20 card tells you what to do.

00:03:25.865 --> 00:03:28.031
You write to us, and we set it up with you.

00:03:28.784 --> 00:03:31.819
To go on, tap Choose under the pass you want.

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:34.662
That opens Stripe's secure payment page.

00:03:34.662 --> 00:03:40.525
We stop here, because this is only a demonstration, and we never enter card details in a video.

00:03:41.369 --> 00:03:46.223
After you pay, your contest is created by itself, with everything you typed.

00:03:46.223 --> 00:03:56.524
Your window runs for twelve months from the day you buy your pass, or the day your first contest goes live if that comes first, and a contest that is unpublished still counts.

00:03:56.524 --> 00:04:01.209
If you need more contests later, choose a bigger pass, and you pay only the difference.

00:04:02.029 --> 00:04:06.593
Entering and voting stay free for everyone, and payment never affects who wins.

00:04:07.427 --> 00:04:10.020
Next up: Create a contest with Quick start.
